{"id":"mahabharata-1-025","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":25,"title":"पञ्चविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 25 · The elephant and the tortoise","summary":{"en":"A Brahmin caught in Garuda's throat burns it, and Garuda releases him with his Nishada wife. Still hungry, Garuda asks his father Kashyapa for food and is told of two brothers cursed to be a giant elephant and tortoise; he seizes them and alights on a huge tree, whose branch breaks under him.","kn":"ಗರುಡನ ಗಂಟಲಲ್ಲಿ ಸಿಕ್ಕ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನು ಉರಿಸಿದಾಗ ಅವನನ್ನು ನಿಷಾದ ಪತ್ನಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಬಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇನ್ನೂ ಹಸಿದ ಗರುಡನು ತಂದೆ ಕಶ್ಯಪನಲ್ಲಿ ಆಹಾರ ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ, ಆನೆ ಆಮೆಗಳಾಗುವಂತೆ ಶಾಪಗೊಂಡ ಇಬ್ಬರು ಸಹೋದರರ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ತಿಳಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವುಗಳನ್ನು ಹಿಡಿದು ದೊಡ್ಡ ಮರದ ಮೇಲೆ ಕುಳಿತಾಗ ಕೊಂಬೆ ಮುರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"गरुड़ के कण्ठ में फँसा एक ब्राह्मण उसे जलाता है, और गरुड़ उसे उसकी निषाद पत्नी सहित छोड़ देते हैं। भूखे गरुड़ पिता कश्यप से भोजन पूछते हैं और हाथी-कछुआ बनने का शाप पाए दो भाइयों के बारे में जानते हैं; उन्हें पकड़कर एक विशाल वृक्ष पर बैठते हैं, जिसकी शाखा टूट जाती है।","te":"గరుడుని గొంతులో చిక్కిన బ్రాహ్మణుడు మంట పుట్టించగా, అతనిని నిషాద భార్యతో సహా విడిచిపెడతాడు. ఇంకా ఆకలితో గరుడుడు తండ్రి కశ్యపుని ఆహారం అడగగా, ఏనుగు తాబేలుగా శపించబడిన ఇద్దరు సోదరుల గురించి తెలుసుకుంటాడు; వాటిని పట్టుకొని పెద్ద వృక్షంపై వాలగా కొమ్మ విరుగుతుంది.","ta":"கருடனின் தொண்டையில் சிக்கிய ஓர் அந்தணன் எரிச்சல் தர, அவனை அவனது நிஷாத மனைவியுடன் விடுவிக்கிறான். இன்னும் பசியோடு தந்தை கஶ்யபரிடம் உணவு கேட்க, யானையும் ஆமையுமாகச் சபிக்கப்பட்ட இரு சகோதரர்களைப் பற்றி அறிகிறான்; அவற்றைப் பற்றிக்கொண்டு பெரிய மரத்தில் அமர, அதன் கிளை முறிகிறது.","ml":"ഗരുഡന്റെ തൊണ്ടയിൽ കുടുങ്ങിയ ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ അതിനെ പൊള്ളിക്കുന്നു; ഗരുഡൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെയും നിഷാദ ഭാര്യയെയും വിട്ടയക്കുന്നു. ഇപ്പോഴും വിശന്ന ഗരുഡൻ പിതാവായ കശ്യപനോട് ആഹാരം ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ആനയും ആമയുമായി ശപിക്കപ്പെട്ട രണ്ടു സഹോദരന്മാരെക്കുറിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹം അറിയുന്നു. അവരെ പിടിച്ച് ഒരു ഭീമവൃക്ഷത്തിന്മേൽ ഇരിക്കുമ്പോൾ അതിന്റെ കൊമ്പ് ഒടിയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.25; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्य कण्ठमनुप्राप्तो ब्राह्मणः सह भार्यया ।\nदहन्दीप्त इवाङ्गारस्तमुवाचान्तरिक्षगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin with his wife had reached Garuda's throat, burning like a glowing coal, and the sky-goer spoke to him."}},{"n":2,"text":"द्विजोत्तम विनिर्गच्छ तूर्णमास्यादपावृतात् ।\nन हि मे ब्राह्मणो वध्यः पापेष्वपि रतः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of the twice-born, come out of my open mouth at once. I may not kill a brahmin, even one always engaged in sin.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"ब्रुवाणमेवं गरुडं ब्राह्मणः समभाषत ।\nनिषादी मम भार्येयं निर्गच्छतु मया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Garuda said this, the brahmin replied, \"This Nishada woman is my wife. Let her come out with me.\""}},{"text":"गरुड उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Garuda said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"एतामपि निषादीं त्वं परिगृह्याशु निष्पत ।\nतूर्णं संभावयात्मानमजीर्णं मम तेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Take this Nishada woman too and quickly get out. Hurry, and save yourself before you are digested by my fire.\""}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः स विप्रो निष्क्रान्तो निषादीसहितस्तदा ।\nवर्धयित्वा च गरुडमिष्टं देशं जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the brahmin came out with the Nishada woman, praised Garuda, and went to the place he wished."}},{"n":6,"text":"सहभार्ये विनिष्क्रान्ते तस्मिन्विप्रे स पक्षिराट् ।\nवितत्य पक्षावाकाशमुत्पपात मनोजवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After the brahmin and his wife had left, the king of birds spread his wings and rose into the sky, swift as thought."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततोऽपश्यत्स पितरं पृष्टश्चाख्यातवान्पितुः ।\nअहं हि सर्पैः प्रहितः सोममाहर्तुमुद्यतः ।\nमातुर्दास्यविमोक्षार्थमाहरिष्ये तमद्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"He then saw his father and, asked by him, explained: \"The serpents have sent me to bring the soma, and I am set to fetch it today to free my mother from slavery."}},{"n":8,"text":"मात्रा चास्मि समादिष्टो निषादान्भक्षयेति वै ।\nन च मे तृप्तिरभवद्भक्षयित्वा सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mother told me to eat Nishadas, but eating thousands of them has not satisfied me."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्माद्भोक्तव्यमपरं भगवन्प्रदिशस्व मे ।\nयद्भुक्त्वामृतमाहर्तुं समर्थः स्यामहं प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, venerable one, tell me of something else to eat, which would give me the strength to bring the nectar.\""}},{"text":"कश्यप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kashyapa said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"आसीद्विभावसुर्नाम महर्षिः कोपनो भृशम् ।\nभ्राता तस्यानुजश्चासीत्सुप्रतीको महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There was a great sage named Vibhavasu, very hot-tempered. His younger brother was the great ascetic Supratika."}},{"n":11,"text":"स नेच्छति धनं भ्रात्रा सहैकस्थं महामुनिः ।\nविभागं कीर्तयत्येव सुप्रतीकोऽथ नित्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great sage Supratika did not wish to keep wealth jointly with his brother, and kept speaking of dividing it."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथाब्रवीच्च तं भ्राता सुप्रतीकं विभावसुः ।\nविभागं बहवो मोहात्कर्तुमिच्छन्ति नित्यदा ।\nततो विभक्ता अन्योन्यं नाद्रियन्तेऽर्थमोहिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then his brother Vibhavasu said to Supratika, 'Many people, out of delusion, want to divide the inheritance. Once divided, deluded by wealth, they stop respecting each other."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः स्वार्थपरान्मूढान्पृथग्भूतान्स्वकैर्धनैः ।\nविदित्वा भेदयन्त्येतानमित्रा मित्ररूपिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing such foolish people, set apart with their own wealth and bent on self-interest, enemies posing as friends cause them to quarrel."}},{"n":14,"text":"विदित्वा चापरे भिन्नानन्तरेषु पतन्त्यथ ।\nभिन्नानामतुलो नाशः क्षिप्रमेव प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others, learning they are divided, find gaps to enter, and for the divided swift and unequalled ruin follows."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्माच्चैव विभागार्थं न प्रशंसन्ति पण्डिताः ।\nगुरुशास्त्रे निबद्धानामन्योन्यमभिशङ्किनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the wise do not approve of division among those bound by their teacher's teaching, who now suspect each other."}},{"n":16,"text":"नियन्तुं न हि शक्यस्त्वं भेदतो धनमिच्छसि ।\nयस्मात्तस्मात्सुप्रतीक हस्तित्वं समवाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You cannot be restrained; you want your wealth through division. Therefore, Supratika, you will become an elephant.'"}},{"n":17,"text":"शप्तस्त्वेवं सुप्रतीको विभावसुमथाब्रवीत् ।\nत्वमप्यन्तर्जलचरः कच्छपः संभविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cursed thus, Supratika answered Vibhavasu, 'You too will become a tortoise moving in the water.'"}},{"n":18,"text":"एवमन्योन्यशापात्तौ सुप्रतीकविभावसू ।\nगजकच्छपतां प्राप्तावर्थार्थं मूढचेतसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So by each other's curse, Supratika and Vibhavasu, their minds deluded for the sake of wealth, became an elephant and a tortoise."}},{"n":19,"text":"रोषदोषानुषङ्गेण तिर्यग्योनिगतावपि ।\nपरस्परद्वेषरतौ प्रमाणबलदर्पितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having fallen into animal births through the fault of anger, they delight in hating each other, proud of their size and strength."}},{"n":20,"text":"सरस्यस्मिन्महाकायौ पूर्ववैरानुसारिणौ ।\nतयोरेकतरः श्रीमान्समुपैति महागजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this lake, huge-bodied, they follow their old enmity. One of them, a splendid great elephant, comes here."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्य बृंहितशब्देन कूर्मोऽप्यन्तर्जलेशयः ।\nउत्थितोऽसौ महाकायः कृत्स्नं संक्षोभयन्सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the sound of his trumpeting, the huge tortoise lying in the water rises, stirring the whole lake."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वावेष्टितकरः पतत्येष गजो जलम् ।\nदन्तहस्ताग्रलाङ्गूलपादवेगेन वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, the mighty elephant plunges into the water, trunk curled, in the force of his tusks, trunk-tip, tail and feet."}},{"n":23,"text":"तं विक्षोभयमाणं तु सरो बहुझषाकुलम् ।\nकूर्मोऽप्यभ्युद्यतशिरा युद्धायाभ्येति वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he churns the lake full of fish, the mighty tortoise too comes with head raised for battle."}},{"n":24,"text":"षडुच्छ्रितो योजनानि गजस्तद्द्विगुणायतः ।\nकूर्मस्त्रियोजनोत्सेधो दशयोजनमण्डलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The elephant is six yojanas tall and twice that long. The tortoise is three yojanas high and ten yojanas around."}},{"n":25,"text":"तावेतौ युद्धसंमत्तौ परस्परजयैषिणौ ।\nउपयुज्याशु कर्मेदं साधयेप्सितमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Maddened by battle and each wanting to defeat the other, they are there. Go quickly, eat them, and accomplish your desired deed.\""}},{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"स तच्छ्रुत्वा पितुर्वाक्यं भीमवेगोऽन्तरिक्षगः ।\nनखेन गजमेकेन कूर्ममेकेन चाक्षिपत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his father's words, the swift sky-goer snatched the elephant in one claw and the tortoise in the other."}},{"n":27,"text":"समुत्पपात चाकाशं तत उच्चैर्विहंगमः ।\nसोऽलम्बतीर्थमासाद्य देववृक्षानुपागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bird rose high into the sky, then reached Alamba tirtha and came to the divine trees."}},{"n":28,"text":"ते भीताः समकम्पन्त तस्य पक्षानिलाहताः ।\nन नो भञ्ज्यादिति तदा दिव्याः कनकशाखिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by the wind from his wings, those golden-branched divine trees trembled in fear, thinking, \"May he not break us.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"प्रचलाङ्गान्स तान्दृष्ट्वा मनोरथफलाङ्कुरान् ।\nअन्यानतुलरूपाङ्गानुपचक्राम खेचरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the trees shake, whose fruits were the sprouts of heart's desires, the sky-goer went to others of matchless form."}},{"n":30,"text":"काञ्चनै राजतैश्चैव फलैर्वैडूर्यशाखिनः ।\nसागराम्बुपरिक्षिप्तान्भ्राजमानान्महाद्रुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were great trees, ringed by the ocean's waters and shining, with branches of lapis lazuli and fruits of gold and silver."}},{"n":31,"text":"तमुवाच खगश्रेष्ठं तत्र रोहिणपादपः ।\nअतिप्रवृद्धः सुमहानापतन्तं मनोजवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A huge, tall Rohina tree there addressed the best of birds as he swooped, swift as thought:"}},{"n":32,"text":"यैषा मम महाशाखा शतयोजनमायता ।\nएतामास्थाय शाखां त्वं खादेमौ गजकच्छपौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Perch on this great branch of mine, a hundred yojanas long, and eat the elephant and tortoise there.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"ततो द्रुमं पतगसहस्रसेवितं\nमहीधरप्रतिमवपुः प्रकम्पयन् ।\nखगोत्तमो द्रुतमभिपत्य वेगवा-\nन्बभञ्ज तामविरलपत्रसंवृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the swift best of birds, shaking the tree, which was frequented by thousands of birds and had a body like a mountain, fell upon it and broke that branch, thick with leaves."}}]}]}